From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenHarmony PC adaptation <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH 2/2] Give the shared library a DT_SONAME on HarmonyOS

Give the shared library a DT_SONAME on HarmonyOS

Upstream sets only

    set_property(TARGET matrix_client PROPERTY SOVERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION})

Measured on the device (CMake 4.1.2, clang 15), that is not enough on OHOS:
the generated link line carries no -soname argument, the built file is an
unversioned libmatrix_client.so, DT_SONAME is absent, and the exported
MatrixClientTargets-release.cmake therefore marks the imported target
IMPORTED_NO_SONAME TRUE. The SONAME quality gate rejects both, and consumers
would have to link by full path -- which in turn bakes a build-machine path
into DT_NEEDED.

A minimal control project on the same toolchain reproduces it: with
`add_library(x)` + VERSION/SOVERSION set, CMake reports
TYPE=SHARED_LIBRARY VERSION=0.10.1 SOVERSION=0.10.1 yet still emits neither a
versioned filename nor a soname flag. This matches the platform behaviour
recorded as E207 in the packaged knowledge base.

The fix sets VERSION and SOVERSION and additionally passes the soname to the
linker explicitly. tcl 8.6.16 and visp 3.7.0 fixed the same gate failure the
same way. The library target's sources and the test set are untouched.
Signed-off-by: OpenHarmony PC adaptation <noreply@example.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 15 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index e337f57..6201403 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -386,7 +386,6 @@ export(EXPORT
 	MatrixClient::)
 export(PACKAGE MatrixClient)
 
-set_property(TARGET matrix_client PROPERTY SOVERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION})
 
 if(BUILD_LIB_TESTS)
 	enable_testing()
@@ -514,3 +513,17 @@ if(BUILD_LIB_TESTS)
 	add_test(Responses responses)
 	add_test(Requests requests)
 endif()
+
+# --- OHOS: force a DT_SONAME -------------------------------------------------
+# CMake on HarmonyOS does not emit -soname for a SHARED_LIBRARY even when
+# VERSION/SOVERSION are set, so the library ships without DT_SONAME, installs
+# unversioned, and the exported import target becomes IMPORTED_NO_SONAME TRUE.
+# Downstream then records a build-machine path in DT_NEEDED instead of a soname.
+# Pass the soname explicitly; the packaged knowledge base records the same
+# platform behaviour (E207) and the same remedy (tcl 8.6.16, visp 3.7.0).
+set_target_properties(matrix_client PROPERTIES
+	VERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION}
+	SOVERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION})
+set(_mtx_soname "libmatrix_client.so.${PROJECT_VERSION}")
+target_link_options(matrix_client PRIVATE "LINKER:-soname,${_mtx_soname}")
+message(STATUS "MatrixClient soname forced to ${_mtx_soname}")

-- 
